CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ elem0 stored: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ elem1 stored: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ elem2 stored: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
N5008 [class.base.init] + [temp.variadic] + [temp.param]/11: a recursive variadic
forwarding constructor (the std::_Tuple_impl shape) whose member-initializer
builds its base from the tail pack, with an enable_if trailing constraint
referencing both the constructor's pack and the enclosing class's pack.  Covers
a parameter pack that is not the last template parameter, `sizeof...(class-pack)`
in a trailing default of a recursively-instantiated constructor, and the empty-
pack terminal recursion.  Each element must be stored at its recursive position;
assertion.4 ("WRONG") must FAIL (non-vacuity).
